 "note": "T2 mud golem. The body (hump with roots and stones, the skull-faced head with the glowing eyes and drooling fangs) is the armless Step-4 edit of the reference (src/mud_body.webp); its base fades out into the separately cut puddle, drawn over it so the golem stands IN the mud (and alone while it swims under the floor). The arm (a single dripping mud limb with its fist) and the mud ball come from parts sheet 2; the arm is rotated so it runs along +x and is drawn as a bending chain (a soft limb that stretches on the punch); its socket opening is cut away and faded into the shoulder. The head is cut as its own part (its back faded into the hump, the body keeps the hump and neck only) so the near arm can swing between the body and the head, and the head can nod and lunge. k: 72 px tall over the 76 px logic rect, arm 33 px, ball 12 px.",
